   This equation shows the balanced reaction between benzoic acid and sodium hydroxide, producing water and sodium benzoate.  

2. **Fully Ionized Equation:**  
   \[ \text{H}_2\text{O} + \text{NaC}_7\text{H}_5\text{O}_2 \rightarrow \text{Na}^+\text{ + H}_2\text{O} + \text{C}_7\text{H}_5\text{O}_2^- \)]  

3. **Observable Effects:**  
   - **Dissolution:** The solid NaOH will dissolve in water, forming hydroxide ions (OH⁻).  
