  - PbO (Pb): 1.9  
  - ZnO (Zn): 1.9  
  - Fe₂O₃ (Fe): 1.8  
- The electronegativity of ZnO (Zn) and PbO (Pb) are close to that of carbon, making reduction by carbon difficult.  
- However, ZnO is more difficult to reduce than PbO because the difference in electronegativity is smaller.  
- The other oxides (Al₂O₃ and Fe₂O₃) have lower electronegativity than carbon, making them more easily reduced by carbon.  

