   - Ethanol has the lowest vapor pressure but the highest PEL, suggesting that it is less volatile but can be tolerated at higher concentrations without significant health risks.  
   - Methanol has the highest vapor pressure and a moderate PEL, indicating that it evaporates more readily and requires careful control to prevent overexposure.  

