   \[
   \ln(A) = -kt + k_0
   \]  
   
   The slope of the plot of \(\ln(A)\) vs. time is \(-k\).  
   
   The rate constant \( k \) for a second-order reaction is given by:  
   \[
   \frac{1}{m(\text{urea})} = \frac{1}{0} + \frac{kt}{m(\text{urea}})
   \]  
