c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The correct classification of each study is as follows:

a) **Retrospective**. The study looks backward to the past (smoking habits) to investigate a relationship with a current condition (bladder cancer).

b) **Prospective**. The study records eating habits and health over a period of time, and then monitors for health outcomes.

c) **Prospective**. The study follows a group of individuals over time, collecting data on their eating and exercise habits and then observing whether they develop cancer later.

d) **Cross-sectional**. This study compares two groups (generic vs. branded items) at a single point in time. It does not involve tracking changes over time.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

