(iii) The time constant.  
(iv) The value of convective heat transfer coefficient up to which the lumped parameter model can be used.  
(v) The volumetric area ratio up to which the lumped partarameter model can be used.  

1. **Given Data**:  
   - Mass (m) = 1.2 kg  
   - Density (ρ) = 7150 kg/m³  
   - Surface area (A) = 0.075 m²  
   - Thermal conductivity (k) = 95 W/mK  
   - Specific heat (c) = 385 J/kg K  
   - Initial temperature (T₀) = 345°C  
   - Ambient temperature (Tₙ) = 20°C  
   - Convective heat transfer coefficient (h) = 56.8 W/m²K  

2. **Calculations**:  
   - **Volume (V)**:  
     \[
     V = \frac{m}{\rho} = \frac{1.2 \text{ kg}}{7150 \text{ kg/m³}} = 0.00166 \text{ m}^3
     \]  
