\[ \Delta \lambda = \lambda_0 (2\alpha) = \lambda_0 \left(2 \frac{h}{m_e c}\right) \]
where:
- \(\lambda_0\) is the wavelength of the incident photon.
- \(\alpha\) is the Compton scattering constant, given by \(\alpha = \frac{h}{m_e c}\).
- \(h\) is Planck's constant \(6.626 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}\).
- \(m_e\) is the mass of the electron \(9.1 \times 10^{-3.1} \text{ kg}\).
- \(c\) is the speed of light \(3.0 \times 10^3 \text{ m/s}\).

