\]

\[
B = \frac{4 \times 10^{-6} \times 100}{0.4} \, \text{T}
\]

\[
B = \frac{400 \times 10^{-6}}{0.4} \, \text{T}
\]

\[
B = 1000 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{T}
\]

\[
B = 1 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{T}
\]

Thus, the magnetic field strength at the center of the circular coil is \( 1 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{T} \).

