","To verify the unitarity condition for the \(S\)-matrix, we consider the sum \(\sum_l S_{lm}^* S_{ln}\). The matrix elements \(S_{lm}\) are defined as \(S_{lm} = \lambda_m \bar{\lambda_l}\), where \(\lambda_m\) and \(\lambda_l\) are the wave functions of the matrix states \(m\) and \(l\), respectively. The matrix \(S\) is invariant under rotation, so it is invariant under the rotation of the matrix elements.

The matrix elements of the \(S\-matrix\) are given by \(S_{mn} = \lambda_m \bar{\l_n}\), where \(\lambda_m\) and \(\lambda_n\) are the wave functions of the matrix states \(m\) and \(n\), respectively. The matrix \(S\) is invariant under rotation, so it is invariant under the rotation of the matrix elements.

The unitarity condition is given by \(\sum_l S_{lm}^* S_{ln} = \delta_{mn}\), where \(\lambda_m\) and \lambda_n\) are the wave functions of the matrix states \(m\) and \(n\), respectively. The matrix \(S\) is invariant under rotation, so it is invariant under the rotation of the matrix elements.

